# Module: deps (dependency-injection seam)
Compile unit for the Forum Backend API.
Generates: `backend/deps.py`

## Role
The single injection seam shared by every route module and the event relay. Declares
FastAPI dependency providers and the shared error envelope — **no endpoints, no business
logic, no queries**. Every route module imports its clients and its caller identity from
here, so there is exactly one place tests override.

## Providers
- `get_supabase()` and `get_redis()` are declared here and **never construct a client**.
  `main.py` creates the real Supabase and Redis clients once at startup and overrides
  these via `app.dependency_overrides`; unit tests override them with a stubbed Supabase
  client and `fakeredis`. A provider that has not been overridden **raises
  `RuntimeError`** — no module may fall back to building its own client, and no
  module-level client global exists anywhere in the backend.
- `get_optional_user_id()` → `str | None` (public reads; `None` when anonymous) and
  `get_current_user_id()` → the caller id, raising `401` with the standard error envelope
  when absent. Both read only the id that the `main.py` auth middleware already resolved
  and stamped on `request.state.user_id` — neither verifies a JWT, and neither reads
  `DEV_MODE`. That decision belongs to the middleware in `main.py` and is made once.
- `ErrorResponse` — the shared error envelope model (`error.code` / `error.message`)
  exactly as `prompts/shared/openapi.yaml` defines it, plus a helper that raises it as an
  `HTTPException` so every route returns byte-identical error bodies. The `429` variant
  carries `resets_at`.

## Settings
Env-backed settings are read from `os.environ` **at request time**, using the `*_ENV`
name constants from `backend/contracts.py` — never a literal env-var string, never cached
at import. `SANDBOX_ALLOWED_HOSTS` is parsed here once per read into a host-glob matcher
(`fnmatch`-style, case-insensitive, matched against the parsed hostname) and exposed as
`sandbox_host_allowed(url) -> bool`, since both `routes/reads.py` and `routes/webhook.py`
enforce the same allowlist and must not drift.

## Modules that do not exist
This is the whole seam. There is **no** `backend.auth`, `backend.config`,
`backend.database`, `backend.db`, `backend.models`, `backend.redis_client`, or
`backend.session` module — do not import from any of them, and do not create one.
There is no ORM: SQLAlchemy is not a project dependency, and Postgres is reached only
through the `supabase` Python client obtained from `get_supabase()`.

